<section class="hero wrap"><div class="hero-top"><p class="eyebrow">I design digital products people can actually use.</p><span class="status">Available for product design work</span></div><div class="hero-grid"><div><h1>I make complex products<br><span>easier to use.</span></h1><p class="hero-copy">I’m <strong>Tatheer</strong>, a product designer focused on SaaS, dashboards and digital products. I work on the messy part between a product idea and a screen that actually makes sense.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#work">See the work <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a><a class="button secondary" href="assets/Tatheer-Ul-Hassan-CV.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View resume <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><aside class="hero-note"><p class="eyebrow">How I usually work</p><ol><li>Figure out what actually needs solving.</li><li>Sort the flow before polishing the UI.</li><li>Then sweat the details.</li></ol></aside></div></section>
<div class="work-strip"><div class="wrap"><small>A selection of products<br>I’ve worked on</small><div class="wordmarks" aria-label="Products"><span>GP Flow</span><span>Lillup</span><span>Snapshot Reviews</span><span>Delil AI</span></div></div></div>
<section class="wrap section" id="work"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Selected work</p><h2>A few things I’ve designed.</h2></div><p>A few projects where the hard part was making the product easier to understand, navigate or use.</p></div><div class="project-grid"><a class="project-card " href="veritas.html"><div class="project-visual"><img src="assets/L2.png" alt="Investor portfolio and sponsor analytics dashboard designs for GP Flow" fetchpriority="high"><span class="go" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><div class="project-text"><div class="project-topline"><h3>Veritas / GP Flow</h3><small>Real estate · Fintech</small></div><p>Two user roles, one investment product — and a lot of information to organise.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Role-based workflows</span><span class="tag">Information architecture</span></div><span class="case-link">Explore the case study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a><a class="project-card " href="snapshot.html"><div class="project-visual"><img src="assets/L3.png" alt="Snapshot Reviews engineering dashboard and responsive mobile screens" loading="lazy"><span class="go" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><div class="project-text"><div class="project-topline"><h3>Snapshot Reviews</h3><small>B2B SaaS · Engineering</small></div><p>A component system and product UI for dense engineering data.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Design systems</span><span class="tag">AI interfaces</span></div><span class="case-link">Explore the case study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a><a class="project-card wide" href="delil.html"><div class="project-visual"><img src="assets/dalil3.png" alt="Delil CRM lead table with contextual contact information side panels" loading="lazy"><span class="go" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><div class="project-text"><div class="project-topline"><h3>Delil AI</h3><small>Sales · CRM</small></div><p>A CRM workspace designed to keep the lead, context and next action together.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Workflow design</span><span class="tag">Data-heavy interfaces</span></div><span class="case-link">Explore the case study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a></div></section>
<section class="approach"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / How I work</p><h2>I don’t start with<br>the pixels.</h2></div><p>Before I design a screen, I want to understand what the person is trying to do and where the current experience gets in the way.</p></div><div class="principles"><article class="principle"><span class="number">01 — FRAME</span><h3>Start with the actual problem.</h3><p>Who is this for? What are they trying to get done? What constraints are we working with? Getting those answers early saves a lot of polishing later.</p><a href="lillup.html">See a research-led project ↗</a></article><article class="principle"><span class="number">02 — STRUCTURE</span><h3>Make the flow obvious.</h3><p>I map the important paths before getting too deep into UI. The goal is simple: when someone reaches a screen, the next useful action should be clear.</p><a href="veritas.html">See a workflow case study ↗</a></article><article class="principle"><span class="number">03 — CONNECT</span><h3>Make the patterns repeatable.</h3><p>Buttons, forms, empty states and edge cases all need to feel like they belong to the same product. That matters even more as the product grows.</p><a href="snapshot.html">See the design system ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap section" id="more-work"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Other work</p><h2>More work, different problems.</h2></div><p>A mix of product, web and app work. Some of these are still in progress, so I’ve kept the links to the original design files.</p></div><div class="work-list"><a class="work-row" href="lillup.html" ><span class="index">01</span><h3>Lillup</h3><div class="description">Learning platform · Research & user flows<span>A closer look at the process</span></div><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="work-row" href="https://www.figma.com/design/jNlI91oTdicodu8qPj7NI6/Website-%7C-Renty-Power--Copy-for-WP-?node-id=15-876" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="index">02</span><h3>Renty Power</h3><div class="description">Rental product · Website & app<span>View Figma file</span></div><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="work-row" href="https://www.figma.com/design/GewrexE2gRYOc8ldhv9eBH/Satlantis---Newest-work--Copy-?node-id=0-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="index">03</span><h3>Satlantis</h3><div class="description">Travel community · Product exploration<span>Work in progress · View Figma file</span></div><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="work-row" href="https://www.figma.com/design/KlVxl6CGu9AHH13ExOFwCD/Figma-Dashboard-Design-v2--Copy-?node-id=0-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="index">04</span><h3>SEO dashboard</h3><div class="description">Search analytics · Dashboard design<span>View Figma file</span></div><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="work-row" href="https://www.figma.com/design/LNQsgw7xfZjyQ524Sc0EEk/Order-Cloud--Copy-?node-id=0-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="index">05</span><h3>Order Cloud</h3><div class="description">Commerce · Shopping experience<span>View Figma file</span></div><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="work-row" href="https://www.figma.com/design/FIvmDvIcMbhipT7aafau80/Sponsor-App--Copy-?node-id=1697-165286" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="index">06</span><h3>Sponsor app</h3><div class="description">Sponsorship · Early freelance work<span>View Figma file</span></div><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="work-row" href="https://www.figma.com/design/v65ELV1tJ0NiFND9TqR3ew/Website-2.0--Copy-for-WP-?node-id=1842-12075" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="index">07</span><h3>Marketing website</h3><div class="description">Web design · Landing pages & blog<span>View Figma file</span></div><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><p class="gallery-note">External design files open in Figma and may require a Figma account.</p></section>
<section class="wrap section" id="about"><div class="about"><div class="portrait-card"><img src="assets/Tatheer.png" alt="Tatheer Ul Hassan" loading="lazy"><div class="caption"><span>Based in Sialkot, Pakistan</span><span>Open to remote work ↗</span></div></div><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / A little about me</p><h2>I like figuring things out.</h2><p>I’m a product designer with experience across business software, learning platforms and digital products. I enjoy projects where the requirements are a little messy and the interface has to bring some order to them.</p><p>I tend to ask a lot of “why this?” questions. My work covers <strong>research, user flows, interface design and component systems</strong>, and I care about what happens when a design leaves Figma and reaches development.</p><p>I also have a background in <strong>medical laboratory technology</strong>, which made me interested in products where information has to be clear and mistakes have consequences.</p><div class="about-details"><div><small>Tools & collaboration</small><span>Figma · Prototyping · Developer handoff</span></div><div><small>Interested in</small><span>Product design · SaaS · Health technology</span></div></div><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tatheer-ul-hassan/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">See my experience ↗</a></div></div></div></section>
